---
import PageTurn from '../components/PageTurn.astro';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { pages } from '../lib/registry';
---

<Page
  {...pages['/about/']}
  kind="ProfilePage"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Start', href: '/' },
    { label: 'About', href: '/about/' },
  ]}
>
  <PageTurn initialChapter="about" navigation />
  <header class="page-intro wrap">
    <h1>Matthew, in person</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      I'm a bioinformatician who drifted into engineering because the analysis
      kept depending on the plumbing. About 10 years later I work across
      software, data and practical AI automation. I still like figuring out how
      something works, and then making it useful to the person who has to live
      with it.
    </p>
  </header>
  <article class="reading">
    <h2>Where I've been</h2>
    <p>
      I trained in biology (B.Sc. Marine Biology, Dalhousie) and then
      bioinformatics (M.Sc., University of Calgary). Research jobs came next:
      biostatistics on genotyping and methylation data at the Douglas Mental
      Health University Institute in Montreal, then sequencing pipelines at the
      University of Calgary's Cummings School of Medicine.
    </p>
    <p>
      Along the way I co-authored a paper in <em>Nature Genetics</em> (2019),
      and my genomics papers have about 176 citations between them.
    </p>
    <p>
      For the last 5 years I've worked as a consultant inside Roche and
      Genentech, a biotech company. I started in scientific data curation, moved
      to test automation for sequencing-instrument software, and now work on the
      infrastructure side of internal AI projects. A few things from that
      stretch I'm proud of:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A natural-language assistant over the Ensembl genomics database that cut
        a routine lookup for bench scientists from about 15 minutes to 15
        seconds.
      </li>
      <li>
        Onboarding guides and live demos for an enterprise AI workspace of
        roughly 5,000 people.
      </li>
      <li>
        A Terraform template that lets a team set up its monitoring in an
        afternoon instead of a sprint.
      </li>
      <li>
        Coding agents for a regulated CI pipeline, kept read-only or
        comment-only so a person still makes every change.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What I do for small businesses</h2>
    <p>
      I help small businesses find one workflow where AI can save real hours,
      then build that piece properly. A typical engagement runs like this:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>We map the workflow as it actually happens, workarounds included.</li>
      <li>
        We pick one bounded change and agree on how we'll measure it before I
        build anything.
      </li>
      <li>
        I build it so you can see what it's doing, with logs and plain-language
        docs, and a person in the loop wherever judgment matters.
      </li>
      <li>
        I hand it over with written ownership, so it keeps working after I've
        gone.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      I work remotely with clients in other countries and time zones. Home base
      is near Edmonton, Alberta, on Mountain time.
    </p>
    <h2>Outside the work</h2>
    <p>
      Disc golf, backcountry ski touring, board games and video games. Ski
      touring is the one that sounds most like my job: you read the snow
      carefully before you commit to a slope. All four give this paper workshop
      some of its personality.
    </p>
    <h2>Work with me</h2>
    <p>
      Got a workflow that eats your week? Tell me about it at
      <a href="mailto:moldach686@gmail.com">moldach686@gmail.com</a> or on
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/matthewoldach">LinkedIn</a>. My code
      lives on <a href="https://github.com/moldach">GitHub</a> and my papers on
      <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=FnctGB8AAAAJ&amp;hl=en">
        Google Scholar
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </article>
</Page>
